# Titan: the vendor's health HAL without its wake alarm, added by 65-extra-init.
#
# android.hardware.health@2.0-service keeps its battery chores on a
# CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM timerfd: every 60 s on the charger and every 600 s on
# battery, and a BOOTTIME alarm wakes the SoC. Overnight on 15-16 Nov 2026
# that was 176 of the phone's 290 wakeups, one every ten minutes, each ending a
# sleep sleepd had just started.
#
# Without CAP_WAKE_ALARM, timerfd_create() fails with EPERM; the HAL logs
# "wakealarm_init: timerfd_create failed" and carries on (healthd_common.cpp
# wakealarm_init(); the same branch is in this vendor binary). It still
# registers IHealth and reads the battery on every power_supply uevent and,
# while awake, on its own poll - it just no longer wakes the phone for it.
# Tested on the phone 16 Nov 2026: no timerfd, IHealth/default registered,
# healthd battery lines as before.
#
# The HAL is kept rather than stubbed as on the Mindphone: while it is absent
# hwservicemanager asks init for IHealth/default once a second.
#
# Same definition as the vendor's, plus override, minus WAKE_ALARM; this file
# sorts after android.hardware.health@2.0-service.rc, so init reads it last.
service health-hal-2-0 /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.health@2.0-service
    override
    class hal
    user system
    group system
    file /dev/kmsg w
